WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.968
-My first guest tonight

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:04.470
is an Oscar, Emmy,
and Tony-nominated actor

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.706
who stars in the new movie
"Stowaway,"

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.074
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:11.077
Here is Anna Kendrick!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.179
Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.480
Hey!

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.149
Anna, welcome.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:18.585
Thank you so much
for doing our show again.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.020
It's so good to see you.
-It's so good to see you.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.188
Thanks for having me.
-Please.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.958
It's been probably, I think,
just over a year

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:27.226
since I talked to you last.
-Yeah, yeah, I think --

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:28.661
Yeah, I saw you, like,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.929
right at the beginning of this
whole thing -- that's right.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.163
-Thank you
for doing the show then

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:32.432
and thank you for doing it now.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:36.001
How -- How have you adapted
to -- to living at home?

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:38.571
-Um. I don't think I've adapted
any better than anybody else.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.006
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.
-But, I mean, I'm --

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:44.110
I'm trying to, like,
keep it moving, keep busy.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.813
I'm -- I'm doing, like,
my COVID workout thing.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.614
Like, I'm --
-What is that?

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:50.550
-I'm just -- I'm just, like,
watching YouTube videos

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.385
of some lady and, like,
trying to follow along,

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:55.622
but, like, because it's
the only thing I have to do,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.756
I've kind of gotten
really into it.

00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:00.827
And I'm like -- I'm like,
"Maybe I'm a hard body.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.495
Maybe I'm, like..."
-Wow.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.930
-I'm a --
Like, honey, I'm an athlete.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.065
-Really?
-And then,

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:09.101
it occurred to me recently that,
normally,

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.404
I would be doing this stuff,
like, in a class full of people

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:14.541
with the full-length mirrors
just to really illustrate

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.743
how much I am not nailing it.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.312
[ Laughter ]
-But until then, like, I am --

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:22.314
Come on, Simone Biles,
I'm coming for you.

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:23.916
-You're ready for the Olympics?
-Like, I'm -- My --

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.252
Oh, my body is poetry in motion.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.954
-Oh, it's a good thing they --
they postponed the Olympics,

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:30.423
'cause I'm coming.
-Wow.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.690
That's what I'm talking about.
-Like, that's where I'm at.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.058
-It's just 'cause there's no --
-Until -- Yeah --

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:34.460
Until things go back to normal,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.696
and I actually see just how
terrible all of the form is.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.897
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.166
-Until then, I'm living
this fantasy. I love it.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:43.169
-I want to talk to you about
your new movie, "Stowaway."

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.104
I'm excited for people
to see this.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:48.040
It's -- It's set in space and...
-Yeah.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.144
-And although you've
never been to space,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.278
your name has gone to Mars.

00:01:53.278 --> 00:01:54.481
Can you explain this?

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.382
And this is
the coolest story ever.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.184
-[ Chuckling ] Okay.
So, this is --

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.954
the director is,
like, really into space,

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:05.992
and before the movie came out,
he -- he gave me --

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:09.528
he actually sent me this --
this thing, where he was like,

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.464
"I got" -- it was crazy --

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:15.434
"I got your name and the name
of all of the cast members,

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:18.237
like, engraved
on the Mars rover."

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.373
And I just was like,
"Wait. What?

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.841
Like, this can't be real.
Holy cr--"

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:25.545
And so, I ended up having to,
like, research what this was,

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.280
and it was one of those things
where it's like --

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.515
it is a lovely gift,
but, first of all,

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.017
now I'm doing research,

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.651
so already I don't like
this gift as much,

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:33.720
'cause it's homework.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.854
-Any gift
that makes you do research...

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.722
-You've given me
the gift of homework.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:40.526
[ Laughter ]
And -- And so, what it is --

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:41.927
Do you guys have --
-Yes.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:42.995
-I think you have, like,
a photo.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:44.230
-I do.
This is the Mars rover.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.098
And this is like --
this is amazing to me.

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.600
This is -- Of course,
this is the Mars rover.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.868
-Incredible.
-Yes.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.370
And now your name
is somehow on here?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.205
-[ Laughs ] Okay.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:56.509
So, there's apparently --

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.711
this is what the article said
that I found in my research,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:03.015
was there are three
fingernail-size chips

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:06.719
on the -- this little placard
on the Mars rover where --

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.488
-And you are one
of the fingernails?

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.056
-I'm one of the fingernails,

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:15.962
but 11 million names are
on these fingernail-sized chips.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.297
-So --
-Yeah, there it is. Just these.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:21.667
-In one of these chips...
-In one of these is my name,

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.136
along with
11 million other names.

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:25.838
Very cool.
-So it's still --

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.573
Technically, your name --
You -- You --

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:30.410
-Oh, technically my name
is in space, guys.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.111
-Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.047
[ Cheers and applause ]
You -- You are on Mars

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.281
as we speak!

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.616
You -- You were told,
and everyone knows this,

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.886
don't ever work with animals,
don't work with kids,

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.654
and -- and someone told you...
-Yeah.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.356
-...don't ever
do a movie in space.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.758
-Well -- Okay, so, yeah.
The --

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.994
There's don't work with kids,
don't work with animals.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.395
A production designer
told me to add,

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:53.266
"Never do a movie in space
or on a submarine,"

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.970
because, apparently, it's like
just miserable to shoot

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.638
because it's so cramped --
like, it's such close quarters,

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:01.107
and you have to get, like,
the crew in there

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.008
and the camera people in there.
-Ohh, gosh.

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:04.009
-And so, you know,
when they're doing these,

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.144
like, tracking shots,

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.445
where they're walking
in front of me,

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:08.281
I'm, like, trying to signal
the camera guy, like,

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.282
"You're going to run
into the thing,"

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:11.384
and it's just very, like...
-Oh, 'cause

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.752
they're just walking, yeah.
-You know.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.220
-That's the tricky thing.
-It's just very claustrophobic.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.121
-They're going backwards, and
they're, like, banging into --

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:17.289
Yeah, you're like,
"No, oh, gosh."

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:18.991
-Yeah.
-So, yeah. Tough job.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.160
-Yeah, this is where
I really found out

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.929
I'm just, like, a klutz.
I just --

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:26.131
I'm capable of breaking
anything, no matter the size.

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:27.666
-Netflix was kind enough
to send us

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:30.002
a few of these moments
[Chuckling] of yours.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.972
So here are a few of Anna's
outtakes from "Stowaway."

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.139
Take a look.
[ Beeps ]

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:36.042
-Ready, and action!

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.116
-Jesus Christ!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.185
-Cut, cut, cut.
-Okay, cut.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.353
[ Beeps ]

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.556
-Ohh [bleep].
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.691
-I'm breaking the ship.
I broke the ship.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:53.959
-Abort, abort!

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:55.261
-[ Laughs ] "Break--
Breaking the ship!

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.629
Breaking the ship!"
-"She's breaking the ship!"

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.729
-"I broke the ship."
-"I'm breaking the ship."

00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:00.533
-No, it's like, "Are you okay?"

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.700
This movie's an intense movie,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.036
like,
an edge-of-your seat movie.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:06.939
Would you like to set it up for
everybody -- what it's about?

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:09.208
-Yeah, so it's --
it's three astronauts

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.977
on a two-year mission to Mars,

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.613
and they have enough resources
for three people,

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:18.251
and about 12 hours
into the flight

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.885
that they cannot
turn around from,

00:05:19.885 --> 00:05:21.721
they discover a stowaway.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.989
And it's kind of the questions
of, like,

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:27.827
how do we all survive together,
and what do we do

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.995
if there's really only enough
oxygen for three of us?

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:31.230
-Ohh.
-So it's the...

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.098
Yeah, it is very, like,
nail-bitey.

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:34.833
-I want to show everyone a clip
from the film.

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:36.402
Here's Anna Kendrick
in "Stowaway."

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.770
Take a look.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.039
-You're gonna be feeling
full gravity on the roof.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:44.009
A little over 200 meters
to the solar panels,

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:47.713
but the higher you go,
the less gravity you'll feel.

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.181
-Roger.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.849
-Do not touch the tether
with the clamps --

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:53.586
it's carrying the power down
from the solar panels.

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:54.854
-Loud and clear.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.655
Don't climb the power tethers.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.858
[ Breathing deeply ]

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:05.631
♪♪

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:12.371
♪♪

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.073
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.542
-How cool is that?!
Anna Kendrick, everybody.

